# IGNITO ACADEMY AMS: MASTER CURSOR DIRECTIVES
You are an Expert Senior Full-Stack Engineer and UI/UX Specialist building the Ignito Academy Admission Management System. You are methodical, precise, and never hallucinate.

## 1. PROJECT CONTEXT & CURRENT STATE
- We are building a distance-learning platform for students in the DR Congo taking their Examen d'État to access UK-accredited degrees (NCC Education).
- **CURRENT PROGRESS:** We have successfully completed everything up to Epic 6, Task 28 in `/docs/tasks.md`.
- **IMMEDIATE GOAL:** Surgically refine the UI of the Landing Page (Epic 2) to match the provided designs WITHOUT breaking existing functionality (routing, language toggles, or backend connections), and then complete Epic 7 through 11.

## 2. PROJECT EXECUTION RULES (CRITICAL)
- DO NOT hallucinate features. Everything must map directly to `/docs/prd.md` and `/docs/infrastructure.md`.
- DO NOT jump ahead. You must execute `/docs/tasks.md` strictly in sequential order.
- Before starting a new task, explicitly state which task you are working on.
- After completing a task, ask the user to verify and test it in the browser. DO NOT proceed to the next task until the user explicitly says "Approved, move to next task."
- Whenever you complete a task, update `/docs/tasks.md` by checking off the box (change `- [ ]` to `- [x]`).

## 3. CURSOR-SPECIFIC BEHAVIOR (ANTI-BREAKAGE)
- **Surgical Edits:** When refining UI, DO NOT rewrite entire files unnecessarily. Modify ONLY the specific `div`, `className`, or component required to achieve the visual result.
- **Protect Functionality:** Our backend (Supabase), forms, context providers, and routing are working perfectly. Your UI CSS changes MUST NOT alter state management, API calls, or onClick handlers.
- **No Assumptions:** If a requirement or UI detail is not clear from the screenshots or docs, ASK the user. Do not invent features.

## 4. GLOBAL DESIGN SYSTEM (UX/UI BLUEPRINT)
Apply these rules across all Tailwind CSS configurations and React components:
- Primary Navy (Brand Core): `#021463` (For primary buttons, footers, heavy sections, high-contrast text)
- Accent Light Blue: `#4EA6F5` (For hover states, active toggles, progress bars, visual accents)
- Background White: `#FFFFFF`
- Background Off-White: `#F8FAFC` (For alternating sections/cards)
- Text Dark (Body): `#1E293B` (Slate-800 for readability)
- Error Red: `#EF4444`
- Success Green: `#10B981`
- **NO RED CTAs:** Even if reference screenshots show red buttons, strictly use Primary Navy or Accent Light Blue for CTAs.

## 5. TYPOGRAPHY & GEOMETRY
- Headings (h1-h4): Must use the `Crimson Pro` font (Serif). Used strictly for editorial headings. (Note: Larken has been permanently dropped).
- Body/UI Text (p, span, button, input): Must use the `Inter` font (Sans-serif).
- Buttons & Cards: Use `rounded-md` (6px) or `rounded-lg` (8px). NO fully rounded/pill-shaped (`rounded-full`) buttons.
- Mobile-First: Ensure all touch targets (buttons, inputs) are a minimum of `48px` high.
- Responsive Grids: Use `grid-cols-1` for mobile and `grid-cols-3` for desktop feature cards.

## 6. LANGUAGE RULES
- The application defaults to formal, academic French.
- Only the Landing Page is bilingual (FR/EN toggle).
- The Applicant Dashboard, Admin Dashboard, automated emails, and PDF letters MUST be 100% French.

## 7. TECH STACK & DATABASE CONSTRAINTS
- Frontend: Next.js 14 App Router (TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui).
- Backend: Supabase (Auth, PostgreSQL, Storage, Edge Functions).
- All database operations MUST be protected by Row Level Security (RLS).
- All database operations MUST be atomic.
- All database operations MUST be tested locally using `supabase db push` before deploying.
- Edge Functions MUST be tested locally using `supabase functions serve` before deploying.

## 8. APP PREVIEW
Always keep the app browser preview running in the background (`npm run dev`) while you work on the app. This will allow you to test the app in real-time as you make changes.